docs {
  ## API explanation
  Step 3 of the booking flow: real bookable slots, in the visitor's own timezone.

  Nothing is stored -- slots are computed per request from the teacher's weekly
  rules, minus booked sessions, minus time off, minus anything starting within
  `BOOKING_MIN_LEAD_HOURS` (12) of now.

  Query params:

  - `date` -- `YYYY-MM-DD`. Defaults to today (school time). A malformed date returns 400.
  - `tz` -- IANA name, e.g. `Europe/London`, `America/New_York`. Defaults to `America/Guayaquil`. An unknown zone returns 400.
  - `days` -- how many consecutive days to return, 1-31. Defaults to 1. Use 7 to fill a week view in one call.

  Post `start_utc` back verbatim as the checkout's `start_datetime`. `label` is
  ready to render; `start_local` is the same instant in `tz`.

  ## API example response
  {
    "success": true,
    "teacher": "Fernando Cordero",
    "timezone": "Europe/London",
    "duration_minutes": 60,
    "days": [
      {
        "date": "2026-09-10",
        "slots": [
          {
            "start_utc": "2026-09-10T13:00:00+00:00",
            "start_local": "2026-09-10T14:00:00+01:00",
            "label": "14:00"
          },
          {
            "start_utc": "2026-09-10T15:00:00+00:00",
            "start_local": "2026-09-10T16:00:00+01:00",
            "label": "16:00"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
}
